From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: steamac <steamac@local>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] vkr: import host memory with another memory type when the
 requested one cannot hold it

With dma_buf emulated, host visible and exportable allocations are shm
imported as host memory, which fails for memory types the driver cannot back
with host memory: the lazily allocated (Metal memoryless) type, and with a
MoltenVK lacking PR #2834 every device-local-only type (mangoapp: "host
memory import is unsupported for memory type 0", "vkAllocateMemory failed:
VkResult -1000072003 ... export types 0x200").  The allocation is
asynchronous: depending on timing the guest sees its blob export fail and
frees the memory, or sees success and goes on to use memory that does not
exist (both killed the context).

Import into the first type that accepts host memory and has the requested
properties apart from lazy allocation, as the shm resource import already
does; the guest keeps its memory type.  Only if there is none the allocation
fails as before.
---
--- a/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_device_memory.c
@@ -521,8 +521,33 @@
       uint32_t type_bits;
       args->ret = vkr_get_host_pointer_memory_type_bits(dev, shm->ptr, &type_bits);
       if (args->ret == VK_SUCCESS && !(type_bits & (1u << mem_type_index))) {
-         vkr_log("host memory import is unsupported for memory type %u", mem_type_index);
-         args->ret = VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
+         /* Some types cannot hold host memory: lazily allocated ones (Metal memoryless),
+          * and every device-local-only type with a MoltenVK lacking PR #2834.  A type
+          * with the same properties (apart from lazy allocation) that can is just as
+          * good.  Only the driver memory type changes; the guest keeps seeing the memory
+          * type it asked for.
+          */
+         const VkMemoryPropertyFlags want =
+            property_flags & ~VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_LAZILY_ALLOCATED_BIT;
+         const VkPhysicalDeviceMemoryProperties *props = &physical_dev->memory_properties;
+         uint32_t substitute = UINT32_MAX;
+         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < props->memoryTypeCount; i++) {
+            if ((type_bits & (1u << i)) &&
+                (props->memoryTypes[i].propertyFlags & want) == want) {
+               substitute = i;
+               break;
+            }
+         }
+         if (substitute != UINT32_MAX) {
+            alloc_info->memoryTypeIndex = substitute;
+            vkr_log("host memory import is unsupported for memory type %u; allocated "
+                    "with memory type %u",
+                    mem_type_index, substitute);
+         } else {
+            vkr_log("host memory import is unsupported for memory type %u",
+                    mem_type_index);
+            args->ret = VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
+         }
       }
       if (args->ret != VK_SUCCESS) {
          vkr_shm_free(shm);
